WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.960
Episode 4 features some of the biggest&nbsp;
reveals in "Peacemaker" so far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.480
Will White Dragon armor up&nbsp;
for a big CGI-heavy finale?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.960
Will Vigilante ever find acceptance?&nbsp;
And what's Murn's ultimate goal, anyway?

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.560
Towards the end of Episode 4, Peacemaker has&nbsp;
a heart-to-heart with Harcourt in the same bar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.240
where the two chatted in Episode 1. After noting&nbsp;
that Leota knew about his difficult upbringing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.600
Peacemaker inquires about his file. Harcourt&nbsp;
eventually admits that Peacemaker's file&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.960
says that White Dragon trained&nbsp;
him to kill from a very young age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.920
and that Peacemaker was involved in his own&nbsp;
brother's mysterious death. Peacemaker is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.560
clearly disturbed that his "friends" have such&nbsp;
intimate knowledge of one of his worst memories.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.960
Returning home, Peacemaker lights up a bong&nbsp;
and dances while "House of Pain" by Faster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.440
Pussycat plays in his trailer. Sadly, the&nbsp;
music appears to be a limited comfort to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.800
the emotionally scarred superhero. A series of&nbsp;
flashbacks show a mullet-wearing White Dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.240
forcing a young Peacemaker to&nbsp;
kill a man tied to a chair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.760
As Peacemaker also remembers killing Rick Flag in&nbsp;
"The Suicide Squad," he collapses to the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.120
where Eagly and Goff study him as he mourns the&nbsp;
loss of his brother many decades earlier. No&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.840
doubt we'll find out exactly who's responsible&nbsp;
for his brother's death in a future episode.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.160
Episode 4 is where we see Leota's natural&nbsp;
ability as an intelligence officer shine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:26.000
Because White Dragon has become such&nbsp;
a haunting force in Peacemaker's life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.200
Leota subtly suggests that Vigilante murder&nbsp;
the white supremacist leader. Her skill at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.240
manipulating Vigilante to do her bidding is&nbsp;
markedly reminiscent of that of her mother, Amanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.000
Waller. However, Leota's skills go well beyond&nbsp;
the manipulation of a psychopath like Vigilante.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.360
Upon returning to the team's headquarters, Leota&nbsp;
and Peacemaker discover that Judomaster has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:54.640
escaped, incapacitated John Economos, and is on&nbsp;
the run. Peacemaker engages Judomaster in a fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.080
but the martial arts master is&nbsp;
suddenly gunned down by Leota.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.960
While Leota is unable to pull the trigger on&nbsp;
a former Secret Service agent in Episode 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.534
the lectures from Harcourt appear to be making&nbsp;
a difference in her willingness to kill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:11.520
"Sure, ignore your God-given natural talent."

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.560
We have to imagine her mother would&nbsp;
be pleased by this development.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.280
As the episode comes to a close, Leota is&nbsp;
seen working late at the team headquarters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.640
when she suddenly recognizes&nbsp;
the logo of a bottling company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.200
named "Glan Tai" on a bulletin board&nbsp;
from the home of Senator Royland Goff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.200
Searching through the contents of Annie&nbsp;
Sturphausen's purse, she finds an access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.840
card for the same business. There's no doubt&nbsp;
this business is connected to the Butterflies.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:42.000
Episode 4 is making something clear: However&nbsp;
vile and hateful Peacemaker's father may be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.120
White Dragon is no fool. Early on in the episode,&nbsp;
Peacemaker retrieves a number of helmets built&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.760
by his father and explains to Vigilante&nbsp;
what his father's "closet" actually is.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.160
"It's a quantum unfolding storage area. It leads&nbsp;
to a dimensional nodule outside of normal space."

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.440
"I guess your dad's pretty brainy for&nbsp;
a racist to make a place like this."

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.400
Later, after succumbing to Leota's&nbsp;
manipulation, Vigilante attempts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:09.120
goad White Dragon into attacking him. Though his&nbsp;
fellow white supremacists follow the bait hook,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.600
line and sinker, White Dragon quickly sees&nbsp;
through the ploy and insists that he talk with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.800
Detective Sophie Song. While he has previously&nbsp;
made his hatred for his son abundantly clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.920
White Dragon's next moves are sure to even further&nbsp;
complicate their relationship. We have to imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.400
that his army of white supremacists aren't&nbsp;
going to take too kindly to Vigilante's attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.680
to murder him, especially given his assumption&nbsp;
that Peacemaker orchestrated it. Not to mention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.000
we'd be very surprised if his supervillain&nbsp;
costume doesn't get some use in the finale.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.400
Around the same time that Vigilante is&nbsp;
released from prison, Murn sits in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.840
apartment watching the laughing&nbsp;
gas scene from "Lethal Weapon 4."

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.080
However, the task force captain appears&nbsp;
entirely emotionless while watching.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.240
Instead of feasting on a bowl of popcorn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:56.480
Murn is revealed to be eating the same amber&nbsp;
fluid found at the home of the Butterflies.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.240
The revelation that Murn is actually&nbsp;
a Butterfly is certainly surprising,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:04.800
but it also makes a lot of sense in the&nbsp;
context of previous events. In Episode 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.800
Murn admits to Economos that he is saddened&nbsp;
by the things he has done in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:14.080
but doesn't go into detail about how he came to&nbsp;
be remorseful and also doesn't appear to be overly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:18.880
emotional about it. Oddly, he notes that it is the&nbsp;
first time he's ever shared a feeling with anyone.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.320
"Come on, you've never shared any feeling."

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:22.820
"Nope."

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.280
"Like you've never even said&nbsp;
like 'oh my god, I'm hungry.'"

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:26.340
"No."

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.520
Later, when Peacemaker describes the purple trunks&nbsp;
coming out of the mouths of the Goff family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.480
Murn doesn't hesitate in delivering an order to&nbsp;
assassinate the senator, his wife and their two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:42.160
children. Murn's Butterfly status also makes this&nbsp;
moment from early in episode 4 highly suspect.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.450
"It's my dad, man, Jesus. Do you have a f---ing dad?"

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.262
"I&nbsp;did. I wasn't created in a petri dish."

00:04:48.262 --> 00:04:51.680
While Murn's exact paternal origins&nbsp;
remain a mystery at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.817
a petri dish no longer sounds&nbsp;
as unlikely as it did before.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.080
Every episode of "Peacemaker" ends with a&nbsp;
post-credits scene that expands on another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.240
scene from the episode that just finished&nbsp;
airing. Episode 4 ends with a return to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.840
White Dragon's quantum unfolding storage area,&nbsp;
where Peacemaker argues with Vigilante over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.400
troubling connection between Peacemaker's&nbsp;
mission and his father's overt racism.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.240
In the original scene, Peacemaker is&nbsp;
angry when Vigilante proclaims that

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:25.680
"If it walks like a duck, it's either a duck&nbsp;
or a duck wearing some kind of human costume."

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.160
Peacemaker insists that couldn't work, noting,

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.400
"A duck in a human costume. The&nbsp;
sizes are completely incompatible!"

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.200
While he points this out in the original scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.840
he goes on at length about&nbsp;
it in the extended edition.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:42.400
"You've had a lot of f---ing&nbsp;
stupid ideas, but a duck in a human costume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:48.320
that's the stupidest idea you've ever f---ing had&nbsp;
and it's offensive to me because I have a soul,"

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.840
This definitely seems like a wink-wink moment from&nbsp;
James Gunn, considering that the size difference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.800
between humans and Butterflies is clearly&nbsp;
not an obstacle to their human disguises.

